meta {
  name: Delete the chapter
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curriculum-nodes/{{mistakenNodeId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  A node with nothing mapped to it deletes cleanly, and takes its children with
  it -- a subtree with no root is a syllabus nobody can navigate.

  A node with a placement on it does not. That foreign key restricts rather
  than cascades, so deleting a taught topic that content has been mapped to
  fails instead of quietly dropping the mapping. The fix is deliberate: move or
  reject the placements first, which is a decision about where that content
  belongs and not something a delete should make on the caller's behalf.

  Deleting a node the caller cannot write to is 404.
}
